Ladybird applies a tab’s force-dark state, resolved for the host of the
tab’s top-level document, in every process that hosts part of the tab.
Chromium does the same with all of the WebPreferences WebContentsImpl
computes for a tab: RenderViewHostImpl::SendWebPreferencesToRenderer()
sends them to the renderer of each frame, out-of-process iframes too,
where WebView::ApplyWebPreferences() calls SetForceDarkModeEnabled().
Gecko and WebKit have no force-dark mode at all.
